// Plan 0058 M1 (Spec 0058 R3, R6; ruling Q8; ADR-0112 D2; J3): the
// atlantis.remote/1 conformance vectors, generated by the C++ implementation
// and committed for every other implementation to check against:
//   - codec_vectors.jsonl: one wire value per line, produced by the C++
//     codec (src/remote/src/codec.h) from a fixed list of values. Another
//     implementation decodes each and re-encodes it to the same bytes. The
//     "AuthoringResult" lines (Plan 0065 P6) are not wire values of their
//     own: each wraps an authoring.* method name and the result it answers
//     ({"method":...,"result":...}) for the C# tests to decode as the
//     session does.
//   - sdk_transcripts.jsonl: per named scenario, the commands the C++
//     Gameplay SDK submits for it (recorded on an InProcess connection,
//     encoded by the same codec). The C# SDK runs the same scenarios
//     against the fixture server and must submit the same commands (R3).
//   - camera_vectors.jsonl (Plan 0064 P4): the E1 editor camera's
//     convention -- view and projection from a pose, the pick ray through a
//     point, and the orbit/dolly navigation -- from the C++ model
//     (atlantis/editor/model/viewport_camera.h, itself pinned to the host's
//     extraction by tests/runtime/editor_camera_convention_tests.cpp).
//     Atlantis Editor App's C# port is held to it. Plan 0068 M1 appends the
//     whole camera: every navigation step, points projected with their depth.
//   - Plan 0068 M1 (ADR-0137 D1), the E3 editor's C# models:
//     picking_vectors.jsonl (pixels, rays through pixels, marker picks),
//     gizmo_vectors.jsonl (decompose/compose, axis directions, drag
//     matrices, snapping, the screen handles with their grabs and drag
//     amounts), world_matrix_vectors.jsonl (world matrices solved over a
//     node hierarchy by the authoring World) and history_transcripts.jsonl
//     (E2's edit history, scripted step by step against a fake target).
// A committed file that differs from what the C++ code produces now fails
// here, with the expected text written to the build tree (the Plan 0057 J4
// pattern); nothing rewrites a committed file.

#include "codec.h"

